	"Description": "Framework for top-down HD-2D games: data-driven world and map, pixel-art sprite looks, sky with a day/night cycle, runtime navigation and camera cutaways; characters, stats, combat, abilities, items and loot; perception and stealth; top-down hero controls (camera, click-to-move, cursor, ability picker); a Slate UI kit (dialogue box, menus, cursor, night shade, toasts, HUD drawing); a self-test runner and automation switches; tools (launcher, test runner, asset and pixel-art helpers). No Unreal assets (they live in the game); every game-specific value comes from the game's data, config or hooks.",
